* ''A timer save signs under its session'' (operator, 2026-11-06, approving the house's defaults). Every change books the session that wrote it, and its save signs under that session; the lock and the stand-down flush first; an unbooked save refuses and waits in memory, never written clear. A crash loses only an edit that never reached a booked save; the vessel reports what has not reached durable storage and promises nothing more. The sealed-store carrier holds it, carried by the b1 lanes' carriers at their land.

